WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.012
Shared database objects should not be mysterious.

00:00:03.012 --> 00:00:07.132
PostgreSQL's information schema can show view names and definitions.

00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:11.537
Run this query and inspect the SQL behind the analytics views.

00:00:11.537 --> 00:00:17.587
Being able to inspect a view helps with debugging, documentation, and change review.

00:00:17.587 --> 00:00:22.852
A standard view stores a query definition, not a separate copy of the rows.

00:00:22.852 --> 00:00:29.492
Treat the selected columns, names, types, and grain as a contract with downstream users.

00:00:29.492 --> 00:00:36.022
Changing that contract can break dashboards or applications even if the underlying query still runs.
